  "honest_reading": "THE STORE CARRIES EVIDENCE, NOT INFERENCE. Of 40 contrasts considered, 28 had ground truth from intervention; 4 of those 28 (14%) moved a test outcome. The best LEARNED single signal over the training half achieves held-out accuracy 0.7857 with sensitivity 0.0 and precision 0.0 -- it predicts 'does not matter' for every row and ties the majority classifier exactly. The one-line STATIC rule ('does it matter if a call site passes that position') catches 3 of 3 positives (sensitivity 1.0) at precision 0.30, which is real signal and too imprecise to act on. So: binding is proven (V27), prediction is not. An earlier version of this metric reported the 0.7857 as a success; it was the majority class, the same error this project made in V25.",
